BedJet Nights brings ideas and logic from Lull into Home Assistant.

A copy of this notice ships inside custom_components/bedjet_nights, so it travels
with the integration when HACS or a manual install copies only that folder.

Lull (https://github.com/rkanjani/lull) schedules a BedJet from an iPhone or an
Android phone. BedJet Nights follows its phase model, the BedJet's per-mode
limits and heat safety table, the four starter schedules, the night curve, and
the way a night is rebuilt from its history. Those parts are adapted from Lull
under its MIT licence:

